      "status": "success",
      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "The main argument of The Science of Getting Rich is that getting rich is not solely dependent on having more capital, talents, or doing different things compared to others [4]. Instead, it is argued that getting rich is the result of doing things in a certain way [1], [2], [3], [4], [5], [6]. The book emphasizes that getting rich is not about saving money or doing things others fail to do; it is about doing things in a specific manner [1], [4]. The author also suggests that getting rich is not influenced by one's environment or the business one is in, but rather by the way one does things [2], [3], [5]. Lastly, the book advises readers to focus on their vision and act now, regardless of their current situation, as long as they are doing things in the right way [6], [7].",
